{
  "id": "T-CARSTACK-DOOR",
  "title": "H-CARSTACK-1 attempt 1 (2026-09-28): the host judged an INDOOR client by its avatar, which the mover snaps to the interior's coordinates (a detached island 700-800 m from the city), so every walk-in beside the host flipped the client to its OWN traffic and every walk-out flipped it back onto the host's ghosts - the stacked cars. Fixed: an indoor player is judged by its last OUTSIDE position, as the host judges itself. (a) The host stands inside his salon; the client walks in and out of that shop and the neighbouring gym 3 times: the host's flip counter for the client and the client's applied seq never move. (b) CONTROL: the client far away -> local; back at the door -> ghost. REPORT per leg: [CarStack] LIFTED / [CarHit] counts. NO save.",
  "preconditions": "Reporter fixture session fx-hq1 (MERGED - vars.keepMerger true): '58 ba:street_fifthavenue' is the host's salon, '60 ba:street_fifthavenue' Client1's gym next door. Dev build with the `traffic` readout tail (host: peers=<pid>:<mode>:<flip seq>; client: mseq=<applied seq> near=<own reading>; both: at=x,y,z). enterbuilding teleports, so each player first enters and leaves its door once to make its last outside position the door. ORACLE NOTE: NullReferenceException carries the `(?<!swallowed )` lookbehind (fx-hq1's own Gley diagnostic).",
